Z||000005||Fformula88||08-12-2001||06:13 PM||||Thanks guys!  I certainly wouldn't expect anybody to start a flame war, but I didn't want to be alone in a one vs. the world discussion either!<P>Fix Or Repair Daily is right!  My Probe really is on its second tranny in just 31K miles, and its starting to die!!<P>BTW, Ford Probes aren't really Ford's at all.  They have Mazda drivetrains shared with the Mazda MX-6 and 626.  That just makes them really expensive Fords to fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||08-12-2001||08:46 PM||||I'm definitely not a Probe fan, but they can take a hell of a beating.  My best friend drives a wrecker part time and hauled a Probe out of a ditch about a month ago.  The Probe hit a patch of standing water, became airborne and flipped over landing on its lid.  The car was destroyed, but the driver walked away with barely a scratch.  That certainly says something for the safety of the Probe.<P>That said, does anyone know reason why Probes were developed/produced?  Mustangs sold well but only to the male gender.  Ford wanted something that would sell to females so the Probe was born.  A Mustang for girls.  Keep that in mind, guys, when you're looking for another car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
